      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:44:1",
      "text": [
        " تَقْلِيمُ الْأَظْفَارِ وَ الْأَخْذُ مِنَ الشَّارِبِ وَ غَسْلُ الرَّأْسِ بِالْخِطْمِيِّ يَنْفِي الْفَقْرَ وَ يَزِيدُ فِي الرِّزْقِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, form Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Sufyan Bin Al Samt, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Clipping the nails, and taking from the moustache, and washing the head with the hibiscus negates the poverty and increases in the livelihood’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Sufyan af-Simt who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Cutting fingernails, trimming the mustache and washing the head with marshmallow plant banish poverty and increases one’s sustenance.’” "
        ]
      }
